---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../config';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Support"
  description="Get help with Pilly medicine tracking, reminders, Pilly Plus, and account deletion."
>
  <section class="support shell">
    <div class="support-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">Support</p>
      <h1>How can we help?</h1>
      <p>Tell us what happened and which iPhone and iOS version you’re using.</p>
      <a class="button primary" href={`mailto:${site.supportEmail}?subject=Pilly%20support`}>
        Email Pilly support
      </a>
      <p class="support-email">{site.supportEmail}</p>
    </div>

    <div class="support-grid">
      <article>
        <h2>Reminders</h2>
        <p>
          In iPhone Settings, open Notifications, choose Pilly, and confirm notifications are
          allowed. Pilly schedules reminders on your device; a network connection is not required.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h2>Pilly Plus</h2>
        <p>
          Open Profile, then Account to review your connected provider and backup state. Use Restore
          Purchases from the Pilly Plus screen if an active purchase is not recognized.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h2>Delete an account</h2>
        <p>
          Open Profile, Account, then Delete cloud account. This removes synchronized records and
          private images. App Store subscriptions must be managed separately in Apple Settings.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h2>Medical questions</h2>
        <p>
          Pilly cannot advise you about a medicine, dose, side effect, interaction, or missed dose.
          Contact a qualified healthcare professional for medical guidance.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
